<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?><!-- What: Xml Declaration. Why: Crawlers expect a sitemap to state its XML version and encoding. How: This declares XML 1.0 in UTF-8 as the file's very first characters. -->



<urlset xmlns='http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9'><!-- What: Url Set Element. Why: A sitemap lists a site's pages inside one url set. How: This uses the sitemaps.org namespace crawlers recognize. --><!-- The app is one page, so the set holds one entry. -->


	<url><!-- What: Home Url Element. Why: The app's only page is its root. How: This wraps the root's address and its crawl hints. -->


		<loc>https://easemylife.app/</loc><!-- What: Location Element. Why: Every entry needs the page's address. How: This gives the root's absolute URL. -->

		<lastmod>2026-07-25</lastmod><!-- What: Last Modified Element. Why: Crawlers come back sooner to a page that changed recently. How: This dates the last meaningful content change, and is updated whenever one ships. -->

		<changefreq>monthly</changefreq><!-- What: Change Frequency Element. Why: Crawlers pace their visits by how often a page changes. How: This hints at a monthly change. -->

		<priority>1.0</priority><!-- What: Priority Element. Why: Crawlers weigh a site's pages against each other. How: This marks the only page as the most important. -->


	</url>


</urlset>
